c values\n- [ ] `IF(condition, trueVal, falseVal)` — conditional\n\n### 7. Range Resolution\n- [ ] `A1:A5` → [A1, A2, A3, A4, A5] (column range)\n- [ ] `A1:C1` → [A1, B1, C1] (row range)\n- [ ] `A1:C3` → 9 cells in 2D block (column-major or row-major)\n- [ ] Range with single cell: `A1:A1` → [A1]\n- [ ] Empty cells in range are skipped in aggregate functions\n\n### 8. Reactive Updates\n- [ ] Changing A1 recomputes B1 when B1 = A1+1\n- [ ] Transitive updates: A1→B1→C1 chain updates correctly\n- [ ] Multiple dependents all update when source changes\n- [ ] Changing a non-dependent cell doesn't trigger unnecessary recomputation\n- [ ] Formula cell that's also a dependency recalculates properly\n\n### 9. Circular Reference Detection\n- [ ] Direct cycle: A1→B1→A1 throws error\n- [ ] Indirect cycle through 3+ cells throws error\n- [ ] Self-reference: A1→A1 throws error\n- [ ] After error, spreadsheet is in consistent state (no partial update)\n- [ ] Valid formulas with no cycles work fine after a cycle error\n\n### 10. `getCells()` Method\n- [ ] Returns Map of all non-empty cells\n- [ ] Keys are cell references as strings\n- [ ] Values are computed values (not raw formulas)\n- [ ] Updates after setting new values\n- [ ] Empty after construction\n\n### 11. Edge Cases\n- [ ] Division by zero produces Infinity or error\n- [ ] Formula with only whitespace after `=`\n- [ ] Invalid formula gracefully handled\n- [ ] Setting cell to empty/overwriting clears formula dependencies\n- [ ] Multiple formulas referencing overlapping ranges\n- [ ] Large ranges work correctly\n\n### 12. TypeScript\n- [ ] No `any` types where specific types are possible\n- [ ] Proper interfaces exported\n- [ ] Builds without errors (`tsc`)\n- [ ] Lints without errors (`eslint`)\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":203,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":26880,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":n